{
  "description": "Documents that write every key of autk-grammar 5.4.0's maps, plots, compute passes, data sources and workspaces, a family to a document, on the tables an upstream Autark node hands on: `lines`, in the default workspace and in `east`, and `towers`, buildings in `east`. views: a map of every layer key, a map of OpenStreetMap elements in a workspace that `workspaces` sets, a plot of every mark with every plot key, a plot of every mark with every key of its colors, ticks, titles and selection, plots of every mark over one colorMapRange, a map and a plot laid out and linked by every layout and link key, and maps of every map, layer and camera key autk-grammar 5.3.0 and 5.4.0 add but a layer's `buildingsZeroHeight`, which a node refuses, each of which an Autark node hands the grammar as written; passes: a compute step's GPGPU and render passes with every pass key, which reach autk-compute, and its windows and clusters passes, which run on autk-core (src/tests/adapters/node/autkEveryKey.test.tsx); data: CSV, JSON, GeoJSON, OpenStreetMap (an extract, and tag sets from an Overpass API the test answers, its `overpass`), join, GeoTIFF, heatmap, SQL, update and drop sources with every source key, and `workspaces`, which a run on the server loads (utk_curio/sandbox/tests/test_autk_server_data_keys.py); checked: an update of a layer by every GeoJSON geometry, with every box, and a map raised on a band of a GeoTIFF (`terrain`), which the agents' document check alone runs. autk-db keeps in a workspace only what lies in the box of the first table loaded into it, and reads a GeoJSON source's boundingBox in the workspace's CRS (World Mercator, metres), so each data document loads its widest table first. Every document passes the agents' document check (backend/tests/test_agents/test_autk_every_key_documents.py). utk_curio/backend/tests/autk_grammar_key_tests.json names these tests for each key.",
